sl groups files by purpose (headers, source code, web pages, documents,
images, audio, video, fonts, archives, Apple II disk images, ...), marks the
ones that stand out in the current directory, condenses runs of numbered
names, and lays the result out in columns that fit the terminal.

A Go port of Thomas A. Phelps' Tcl script sl (2012), whose home page is
offline. Tcl hooks are replaced by external commands (--annotate) and the
startup file by a configuration file created on the first run.
